            <ArticleTitle>[Acute low back pain induced by calcifying nucleopathy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>569-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">The nucleopathy calcifying of the inter vertebral disk is mostly asymptomatic.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE RECORD" NlmCategory="METHODS">We report a cave miming a spondylodiscit.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DISCUSSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Although idiopatic in most case, it is necessary to look for a calcifying metabolic disease. The treatment base on the immobilization of the spine and non steroidal anti inflammatory medications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
